FOR HEALTH STUDENTS:

          ※ An essential study aid for medical, pharmaceutical, nursing and scientific examination training;

          ※ The ideal companion for medication leaflets and pharmacology books;


FOR HEALTHCARE PROFESSIONALS:

          ※ Having trouble remembering alpha-2 adrenergic agonists and alpha-1 antagonists? Update the fundamentals that you may have forgotten in college and that you often need to remember in daily practice;

          ※ Stay up to date with the latest drug technologies approved by the FDA and EMA until 2024;


AS REFERENCE:

          ※ Search for alternative medicines by pharmacological classification - essential during drug shortages to find clinical alternatives;

          ※ Create bookmarks and notes for each medicine;

          ※ Filter types of pharmaceutical, supplements and herbal medicines;

          ※ Links to FDA and EMA to quickly find relevant information from reliable sources;


FOR LEARNING:

          ※ Pharmacology Questionnaire - Reinforce the pharmacological classification of medicines;

          ※ Medicinal Chemistry Quiz - Reinforce Structure-Activity Relationships (SARs);

          ※ Practice classifying medicines and identifying structures for a few minutes a day - A little regular practice has been proven to improve recall and reinforce learning;

          ※ Monitor your learning progression across 15 systems and over 2,000 pharmacological classifications. Review previous test results to reinforce memorization;

          ※ Not sure about any pharmacological classification? - Artificial Intelligence integrated into the application will help you explain all pharmacological and chemical terms;

          ※ Create your own personalized drug structure identification/classification quiz in seconds - choose from 15 systems and over 2,000 pharmacological classifications including infectious diseases, cancer, and genetic and metabolic disorders;


TO ALL:

This App is your ideal companion for medication leaflets and pharmacology books, allowing quick reference, finding alternative medicines by pharmacological classification, helping you develop the fundamentals of pharmacology and medicinal chemistry that are essential in making clinical decisions effectively.


